PART 2 – ADDITIONAL TERMS (permitted under AGPL v3, Section 7)
==============================================================================

The following additional terms apply to all use, modification, and
distribution of this software:

1. SPECIALIZATION SIGNATURE VERIFICATION

   The signature verification mechanism located in
   `backend/security/signatureVerifier.ts` (and any successor files)
   is a core integrity feature of this software.

   You MAY NOT:
   - Remove, disable, bypass, or circumvent the signature verification
   - Modify the public key embedded in the verifier to accept
     signatures from any key other than the original author's
   - Set SKIP_SIGNATURE_VERIFICATION=true in any production environment

   Any such modification voids your right to use this software under
   this license and constitutes copyright infringement.

2. SPECIALIZATION FILES (.ari-spec)

   Specialization files distributed by the original author are
   proprietary content, separately licensed, and NOT covered by
   the AGPL. You may NOT redistribute, resell, or reverse-engineer
   signed specialization files.

3. COMMERCIAL USE

   Commercial and non-commercial use of the software is permitted
   under the AGPL, including self-hosting for paying customers,
   provided all AGPL obligations are met.

   This does not grant any right to redistribute, resell, or
   reverse-engineer signed specialization files (.ari-spec), which
   remain proprietary under Section 2.

4. ATTRIBUTION

   All distributions, forks, or hosted instances must retain visible
   attribution: "Powered by A.R.I. © Andre Zabel".

